 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished first, with a score of 2063.7 against 1956.9 for gemini-4-argon in second.\n\nIt was close, and the win depended partly on gemini's population collapsing in the last 1,500 ticks:\n\n- **Early game (to tick ~3000):** large radius-14 organisms with jaws built the lead, peaking near 6,900 biomass.\n- **Mid game:** the big bodies starved once small armoured swarms depleted the sugar, and were extinct by tick ~6500. Radius-6 grazers kept biomass between about 850 and 1,750 through ticks 4500\u20137000, but my lead shrank each window.\n- **End game:** biomass fell to 242 at tick 8500 with the lead down to 37. A late release of lean radius-3 organisms reproduced quickly just as gemini crashed from about 1,200 biomass to near zero, which restored the margin."
